---
layout: page
theme: rubylearning
title: Ruby & Rails Blog
permalink: /blog
description: Fresh lessons, tips, and project write-ups for Ruby and Ruby on Rails developers.
breadcrumbs: true
---

<h2 class="section-title">Latest Posts</h2>

{% assign posts = site.collections.posts | default: empty | reverse %}

{% if posts.size > 0 %}
  <div class="post-grid">
    {% for post in posts %}
      <article class="post-card">
        <h2><a href="{{ post.permalink | url_for }}">{{ post.title }}</a></h2>
        <div class="post-meta">
          {% if post.date %}
            <span class="post-date">{{ post.date | date: site.date_format }}</span>
          {% endif %}
          {% assign top_tags = post.tags | slice: 0, 3 %}
          {% for tag in top_tags %}
            <span class="post-tag">{{ tag }}</span>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        {% if post.description %}
          <p>{{ post.description }}</p>
        {% elsif post.summary %}
          <p>{{ post.summary }}</p>
        {% endif %}
        <a class="read-more" href="{{ post.permalink | url_for }}">
          Read more
          <span class="icon-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span>
        </a>
      </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
{% else %}
  <p>No blog posts yet&mdash;check back soon, or subscribe to the newsletter on the resources page.</p>
{% endif %}

<section class="chapter-section">
  <h2>Stay updated</h2>
  <p>Subscribe to the RSS feed (coming soon) or join our mailing list to hear when new Ruby and Rails guides go live. Have a topic request? Open an issue on GitHub and we&rsquo;ll add it to the queue.</p>
</section>
